illustrates → Problem; involves → ST-01, ST-02, ST-03, ST-04, SA-02; addressed-by → F1, IDP-02, TECH-05.

= Problem Scenario - Nobody to talk to [PS-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|PS-06
|Name|Nobody to talk to
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|(((
Provisional. Constructed from SA-01 and the a2.1 records. No resident or care worker has confirmed it.

* Victor (2012): loneliness in care homes is common
)))
|Narrative|(((
For years he walked his dog twice a day and chatted at every gate. In the care home he walks the garden loop alone. Nobody to talk to; he tells the bench the same story twice. The walks get shorter.

By winter he no longer goes out, and sits by the window. Staff notice only when his mood drops and his legs weaken.
)))
|Stakeholders involved|(((
* ST-01: Resident with dementia
* ST-04: Care worker
* ST-05: Activity coordinator
)))
|Activities involved|SA-01: A walk on your own
|Breakdown point|Without company the walk loses its reason, and the resident withdraws
|Causes|(((
Root causes:

* Loneliness
* No partner who fits; family far away
* The walk had a purpose (the dog, the neighbours) that is gone

Contributing causes:

* Staff time
* Gradual withdrawal is hard to see
* Fear of slips in company
)))
|Sub-problems|(((
1. Company: nobody to talk to
1. Reason: the walk loses its purpose
1. Notice: withdrawal is seen late
1. Bridge: no route from walking alone to walking with someone
)))
|Out of scope|(((
* Treating low mood - ST-06
* Visiting arrangements of families
)))

